From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Fri Jun 17 21:48:51 2016
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Fri, 17 Jun 2016 21:48:51 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] Scanone: some markers change names, need to retain original marker names
Message-ID: <YjXZY_xlEc8.PdYEwObVAQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <YjXZY_xlEc8.4W2nmSDRAQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <YjXZY_xlEc8.4W2nmSDRAQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/YjXZY_xlEc8/m/PdYEwObVAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

scanone performs calculations at the markers plus at positions between markers ("pseudomarkers") at a density defined by the step argument in calc.genoprob (or, for method="imp", sim.geno).

You could rerun calc.genoprob with step=0, and then rerun scanone, and the results will not include any such pseudomarkers.

Or you could remove them afterwards by subsetting with your marker names, or search for the pattern c[chr].loc[pos]. Here's an example.

   data(hyper)
   hyper <- calc.genoprob(hyper, step=1)
   out <- scanone(hyper)

   # use marker names
   out_onlymarkers_1 <- out[markernames(hyper),]

   # search for pseudomarkers to remove
   out_onlymarkers_2 <- out[!grepl("^c.+\\.loc-*[0-9]+", rownames(out)), ]

karl

